{#- A world of its own inside the page — a slide, a printed page, a mail as
    it will be read: what it holds is drawn in a shadow root, where no rule of
    the page enters and nothing is inherited from it, neither the font, nor
    the scheme, nor the skin. What it holds brings its own style, in a
    `<style>` of its body. From outside, only the box it stands in is set: its
    size, its place, its shadow.

    The body waits in a template until the script moves it into the root: a
    template is inert, so nothing of it is drawn, or styled by the page, in
    between. -#}
{%- set slots = slots|default({}) -%}
<div class="isolated{{ class|default(null) ? ' ' ~ class : '' }}"><template>{{- slots.body|default('')|raw -}}</template></div>
